# TOOLS.md — your tools & credentials reference (example)

Copy this to `TOOLS.md` and fill it in with **your** tools. It's injected into the
owner's sessions (see `CLAUDE.md` → "This Session"), so the assistant knows which
CLIs it can call and where credentials live.

> **Never put secret values in this file.** Keep secrets in `.env` or a gitignored
> `secrets/` dir and only *reference* them here. `TOOLS.md` itself can stay private
> too if you'd rather not commit your tool list.

## Secrets convention

- All credentials live in `secrets/*.env` (gitignored) or the bot's `.env`.
- This file *names* a tool and *points at* its secret — it never contains the secret.
- Read a secret by its exact path when you need it; never bulk-scan the `secrets/` tree.

## The CLI toolbelt (`src/tools/`)

These are how the assistant *acts* in Telegram mid-turn — standalone CLIs it shells out to via Bash.
Sanitized examples ship in the skeleton; they read the bot's `.env` for `BOT_TOKEN`/`CHAT_ID`.

- **claw-say** — post or edit a message. `claw-say --progress "⏳ 40% · …"` manages **one**
  self-updating status line per turn (the only thing you should use for progress).
- **claw-react** — set/clear an emoji reaction on a message.
- **claw-mermaid** — render Mermaid diagram code to a PNG (so a diagram shows as an image, not source).
- **claw-host** — upload a local file to object storage and print a public URL (for inline `![](url)`).
  Creds: `secrets/host.env` (e.g. an S3/R2/Cloudinary bucket).
- **claw-ask** — post a poll / quick-reply and collect the answer.
- **claw-task** — delegate a parallel sub-agent and fold its result back in.
- **claw-monitor** — arm a detached watcher (pid/file/log) that wakes a fresh turn when a job finishes.

## Telegram rich-output toy box

Replies render as native Telegram rich text. Beyond Markdown, the sender understands:
- `<tg-time unix="…" format="wDt">…</tg-time>` — live, viewer-timezone date/time (use for deadlines).
- `<tg-map lat="…" long="…" zoom="14"/>` — inline location map.
- `![](https://… "cap")` — remote image/video/audio inline.
- `<<FILE: /path | cap>>` — a local file as its own bubble; `<<INLINE: /path | cap>>` — local media inline.
- `{{react:EMOJI}}` — set a reaction on the triggering message; `{{silent}}` — post nothing, just "seen".

## Example integrations (replace with your own)

- **gh** — GitHub CLI. `gh pr list`, `gh run list`. Auth via `gh auth login`.
- **&lt;email-cli&gt;** — read/triage the inbox. Creds: `secrets/email.env`.
  e.g. `mail search "in:inbox is:unread"`
- **&lt;calendar-cli&gt;** — list/create events. Creds: `secrets/calendar.env`.
- **&lt;music-api&gt;** — now-playing / listening stats. Creds: `secrets/music.env`.
- **curl · node · python3 · git · ffmpeg** — general-purpose, no creds.

## Telegram targets

- Chat id: `<your supergroup id>` (also in `.env` as `CHAT_ID`).
- Topic id → name mapping lives in `src/config.ts` (`TOPICS`) — keep that the source of truth.

## Notes / gotchas

- Document anything future-you will forget: rate limits, token TTLs, odd flags.
- If a service needs periodic re-auth, write down **how** here — so a 3 a.m. session
  isn't stuck guessing.
